# Files owned by the user — fern generate will not overwrite these.
cli/hedra/custom.rs
README.md

# Hand-fixed runtime file: serializes the PAGER env-var tests (flaky in CI).
# The fern-cli-generator runtime doesn't carry this fix yet; regeneration
# must not revert it. Drop this entry once the fix lands upstream.
src/pager.rs

# Cargo.toml stays generator-owned (#25) — fern-config sets `packageIdentity`, so
# regeneration writes hedra-cli's crate identity. Cargo.lock does NOT: the
# generator emits one, but it is resolved from a stale snapshot rather than from
# the manifests it ships in the same run. #29 emitted a lockfile missing `chrono`
# — a direct dependency of an unmodified hedra-sdk/Cargo.toml — along with the
# whole gzip transitive set, so `cargo check --locked` refused it. Pinning the
# lockfile here keeps the good resolution instead of letting each regeneration
# clobber it. (ENG-10048 tried the opposite in #27; this is that experiment's
# result, not a return to an untested assumption.)
#
# Known edge, ENG-10130: the generator stamps the release version into both
# Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock, so a version bump moves the un-ignored manifest and
# not this pinned lockfile — refresh with `cargo fetch` when that happens.
Cargo.lock

# Release pipeline (cargo-dist) + CI + Dependabot are hand-maintained.
dist-workspace.toml
.github/

# The generator never emits .gitattributes — which is exactly why this entry has
# to stay. For a file that exists in the repo but is not emitted, .fernignore is
# the only thing stopping regeneration from DELETING it: PR #29 removed the file
# outright once the entry was dropped. "Never emitted" makes an entry
# load-bearing, not redundant; only a file that is both unemitted and absent is
# safe to un-ignore.
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# The wire-contract harness. The generator never emits `tests/`, which is
# exactly why this entry is load-bearing: for a file that exists but is not
# emitted, .fernignore is the only thing stopping regeneration from DELETING
# it (see the .gitattributes entry above and PR #29).
tests/